WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:09.763
Did it work?

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:13.829
Hello Internet.

00:00:13.829 --> 00:00:20.080
Welcome to Film Theory, the show *who’s
your favorite fearless theorist* You guys

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.460
see Puss in Boots: The Last Wish?

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.460
Review in a word.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.460
Wow!

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.899
We have come a long way from the original
Puss in Boots.

00:00:32.903 --> 00:00:36.360
Needless to say, I did not go in expecting
this new movie to be all that great.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.180
But DreamWorks basically kicked down the door
and said.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.250
The story's wholesome.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.250
The characters are immediately iconic.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.030
And the animation; man!

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:49.220
Between this film, Into the Spider-Verse and
Mitchells versus the Machine.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:52.760
Mickey and the gang got to be quaking in their
boots.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:53.760
Mouse in boots.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.680
In case you haven't seen it yet, the Last
Wish follows our hero cat as he realizes that

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.329
he's on the last of his nine lives.

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:03.739
And so he goes on an adventure to find a fallen
star that will help him wish those lives back.

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:06.030
But Puss isn't the only one who wants that
wish.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:11.759
His former partner Kitty Softpaws, Goldilocks
and her three bears crime family and the unapologetically

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:15.213
evil pie baron Big Jack Horner are all after
it, too.

00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:22.060
I love this guy.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.110
He is one of my all time favorite villains.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:27.760
And if that wasn't bad enough, a mysterious
hooded wolf wants to claim Puss’s his last

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:28.760
life for himself.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.497
Why?

00:01:29.497 --> 00:01:30.194
Well, because he’s Death.

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:41.479
Yup.

00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:45.280
The physical manifestation of death itself
is after Puss in Boots because he doesn't

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.049
feel like Puss has respected the lives that
he's been given.

00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:52.928
That said, all of this about wishing for more
lives and Death chasing him, it's all a moot point.

00:01:52.928 --> 00:01:54.310
Puss should already be dead.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.420
His ninth life is long gone.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.189
Forget the Tumblr sexy man wolf or pie boy
over there.

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:01.000
The biggest threat is Puss himself.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.590
Based on everything that we see from him in
this movie, he'd be dead multiple times over.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.780
By my count, we're talking at least seven.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:11.690
And I don't mean stuff like riding explosive
fireworks or getting thrown into signs that

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.590
crashed through windows or anything like that.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:18.190
No, you see, loyal theorists, almost every
choice that Puss makes endangers his life.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:21.970
Death is absolutely right about Puss playing
it fast and loose with these lives.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.060
But we're not talking about the big picture
adventuring stuff.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.569
I'm talking about all the mundane, everyday
things that’s slowly killing this cat.

00:02:28.569 --> 00:02:31.060
Puss in Boots is wasting his final life.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.710
And I'm about to prove it to you.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:35.409
Grab your star maps and your therapy dogs,
loyal theorists.

00:02:35.409 --> 00:02:37.019
It's time to dive in.

00:02:37.019 --> 00:02:40.350
First of all, let's just start with what we
see Puss in Boots eating throughout the film.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:45.240
See, Puss eats and drinks a lot of stuff that
would be super unhealthy for a cat.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.540
And before you jump down into the comment
section telling me that this is just a cartoon

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:52.250
with a magic cat MatPat, you need to stop
taking all these things way too seriously.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:54.330
First off, do you know what channel you're
on?

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:58.030
Secondly, though, we absolutely should be
taking a look at what Puss is eating and drinking

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:02.220
because we already know that it straight up
was the cause of one of his deaths.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.610
During that opening montage.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:06.799
Puss Eats… eats shellfish.

00:03:06.799 --> 00:03:08.940
During this opening montage, Puss eats shellf..

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:09.940
Wow.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.360
That is… that might be one of the hardest
tongue twisters in a long time.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.360
During that opening montage, Puss eats shellfish
and dies as a result.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.360
WOO did it!

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.860
Now it's played for a joke in the movie.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.190
But shellfish allergies are definitely a thing
that can happen to a cat.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.720
In fact, many of the symptoms are similar
to what we see Puss dealing with in the film

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.470
Hives, as well as swelling of the face and
limbs.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:32.590
Admittedly, death is a bit of an extreme reaction
to having this allergy.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:37.090
Normally, symptoms for cats are more mild,
including hair loss, rashes, blisters, scratching.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:41.129
Though some cats do experience respiratory
problems as a result of the swelling, which

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:42.420
can lead to their death.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.540
Why am I bringing all that up?

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.990
Well, because it shows us that Puss in Boots
is sensitive to this kind of stuff.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.599
And throughout the movie, we see him consuming
a lot of stuff.

00:03:49.599 --> 00:03:51.580
That would be a no go for a cat.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.700
Firstly, we're talking about Puss’s drink
of choice, creme. or milk, I suppose.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.640
We see him drink a lot of it throughout the
movie.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:02.560
It almost seems to have this alcoholic property
for Puss, but that's not how real cats react

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.560
to drinking milk.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:07.996
According to the People's Dispensary for sick
animals, milk can be bad news for our feline friends.

00:04:07.996 --> 00:04:10.230
See, adult cats are lactose intolerant.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:13.870
Their intestines don't have the enzyme lactase,
which would help them break down the sugars

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:14.870
in milk.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.770
And even if they could physically drink it,
you probably shouldn't be giving your cat

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:18.810
milk anyway.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.260
Milk is full of fat.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.449
Basically a saucer worth of milk would be
the equivalent of a human eating an entire

00:04:23.449 --> 00:04:25.479
12 inch pizza in a day.

00:04:25.479 --> 00:04:29.119
And look at how much we see Puss in Boots
drinking in just this movie alone.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:39.850
Do you see all those empty glasses on the
bar?

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:43.810
From this aerial wide shot I count at least
eight empty glasses, plus the one that he's

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:44.810
working on.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:45.833
And Puss isn't even done.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:52.880
That right there is the equivalent of Puss
eating nine plus full pizzas worth of fat

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.060
in just one sitting.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.250
And this is coming the day after he had yet
another milk binge.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:01.291
So despite what all the old cartoons said
about giving your cats milk as a treat, do

00:05:01.291 --> 00:05:02.291
not do it.

00:05:02.291 --> 00:05:06.905
It is just super unhealthy and can lead to
cats becoming overweight and/or their early death.

00:05:06.905 --> 00:05:08.770
So chalk up one extra death for Puss.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.819
He met his maker through milk.

00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:12.465
But perhaps even worse than the milk.

00:05:12.465 --> 00:05:13.280
Coffee.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:21.130
The opening fight against the giant of Del
Mar we see Puss do this.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:25.080
Caffeine is really unhealthy for cats to the
point that it can be seriously dangerous for

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.030
them to consume considering their smaller
bodies.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:31.590
If you want to know more about how crazy dangerous
caffeine can be in higher doses with humans,

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.150
we actually just did a video about that over
on Food Theory.

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.150
But for a cat?

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.720
Side effects from a cat consuming caffeine
includes an increased heart rate, abnormal

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:41.260
heart rhythms, vomiting, diarrhea, tremors
and seizures.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:45.500
According to the Pet Poison Helpline, a moderate
amount of coffee can easily cause death in

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.860
small dogs or cats.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.850
Now, before you start freaking out and hiding
all your coffee in a locked box away from

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:54.282
your animals, a small sip of coffee probably
wouldn't impact a young, healthy animal too much.

00:05:54.282 --> 00:05:59.310
But Puss isn't that young anymore, so downing
an entire cup of coffee like we see?

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:03.310
that is going to be bad news for this animal
and might literally have been the end of him

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:05.979
if the bell didn't crush him to death mere
minutes later.

00:06:05.979 --> 00:06:07.680
Caffeine overdose, death number two.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.169
But it's likely that puts would have died
long before this movie.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:13.486
In fact, he would have died during the promotional
tour for this movie.

00:06:18.109 --> 00:06:18.873
Are you kidding me?

00:06:18.873 --> 00:06:22.600
A fictional cat got onto Hot Ones before me.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:23.550
Screw that noise.

00:06:26.518 --> 00:06:29.000
No, but he's killing me Puss, he's killing
me.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.562
But, yeah, he's probably killing you, too.

00:06:30.562 --> 00:06:34.660
You see, the capsaicin in hot sauce is, as
you might guess, dangerous for cats.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.060
With studies showing that it can constrict
breathing, cause severe irritation in the

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:41.259
throats and digestive system and in high enough
doses cause death.

00:06:41.259 --> 00:06:45.349
And when you're talking about a 2 million
Scoville hot sauce, yeah I'd say that's a

00:06:45.349 --> 00:06:47.360
fairly high dose for a feline.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.874
And then, of course, you have the literal
tankard of milk.

00:06:56.630 --> 00:07:01.259
Hot Ones: Taking out Puss’s life before
he even knew he needed a last wish.

00:07:01.259 --> 00:07:02.970
Capsaicin calamity: death number three.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:06.750
Seriously, Sean, when you do eventually have
me on, I promise I won't make a mess of your studio.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:07.662
So, okay.

00:07:07.662 --> 00:07:11.629
Clearly Puss has himself some dietary issues,
but there are other choices that he makes

00:07:11.629 --> 00:07:14.340
that probably would have gotten him killed
a lot sooner.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.159
Specifically the whole “In Boots” thing.

00:07:16.159 --> 00:07:16.711
Sure.

00:07:16.711 --> 00:07:20.389
Your drip may be on fleek there, Puss, but
you should not be wearing all these clothes

00:07:20.389 --> 00:07:21.730
in your particular line of work.

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:25.379
I don't know if you've ever tried to dress
up your cat, but they do not enjoy it.

00:07:25.379 --> 00:07:29.349
In fact, a lot of experts recommend against
dressing up your cat at all, mostly because

00:07:29.349 --> 00:07:33.123
it causes them a lot of stress with no real
benefit other than some fake internet points

00:07:33.123 --> 00:07:33.876
for you.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:43.577
But even if Puss is the exception here and
enjoys his clothes, his attire will have deadly consequences.

00:07:43.577 --> 00:07:45.490
Let's just start from the top, shall we?

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:46.830
First of all, the hat.

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:50.470
This one item of clothing would probably get
Puss killed for two different reasons.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:54.099
First, by wearing a wide brimmed hat like
Puss does in the series, he wouldn't be able

00:07:54.099 --> 00:07:55.970
to take full advantage of his whiskers.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:58.580
You see, cats don't see the world the same
way that we do.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:02.379
They have a whole suite of abilities to help
them sense what's around them, and their whiskers

00:08:02.379 --> 00:08:04.169
are a crucial part of that system.

00:08:04.169 --> 00:08:09.129
The whiskers act like a sort of radar able
to sense changes in air currents, vibrations

00:08:09.129 --> 00:08:10.129
in the air.

00:08:10.129 --> 00:08:13.250
They also serve as the first level of alert
if anything gets too close to their face.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:16.950
Additionally, while a cat's long distance
eyesight is good at very close distances,

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:20.259
they struggle to see anything that's closer
than 30 centimeters in front of them.

00:08:20.259 --> 00:08:23.629
As a result, their whiskers help them navigate
that close up world.

00:08:23.629 --> 00:08:27.449
By touching the whiskers against objects,
they can tell where things are, how big they

00:08:27.449 --> 00:08:28.879
are, even sensing their texture.

00:08:28.879 --> 00:08:31.860
But the hat is going to stop all of that from
happening.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.280
It's going to change the airflow.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:34.630
It's going to change vibrations.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:37.640
It's going to prevent Puss from getting his
face close to objects so his whiskers can

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:38.640
touch them.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:42.589
Basically, the hat is going to be dulling
one of his most important senses, or I suppose

00:08:42.589 --> 00:08:45.130
I should say two of his most important senses.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:46.890
You notice what else that covers?

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:47.890
his ears.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:51.540
That would be a problem, regardless of whether
you're talking about a human or an animal.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:55.360
Basically, you're just muffling the sound,
allowing enemies to more easily flank or sneak

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:59.150
up on you almost exactly like we see death
do in the movie.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:02.300
If Death here didn't want to be so dramatic,
he could have killed Puss and gone about his

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.610
business without the cat being any the wiser.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:08.690
But the dulling of his hearing is actually
worse for Puss because he's a cat.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.860
You see, cats have some of the best hearing
of pretty much any animal you're going to

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:15.620
have around the house with a wider auditory
range than both humans and dogs.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.140
But we're not just talking about better hearing
ranges.

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:22.200
Cats have a lot of muscle control over their
ears and they're able to turn their ears towards

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.200
any source of sound.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.950
I don't know if you've ever noticed that with
any cats that you know, but if you make a

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:30.100
sound in a quiet room, just notice how their
ears are able to pivot in your direction like

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.070
a big antenna or a radar disk.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:37.161
This cool technique increases their hearing
sensitivity by 15 to 20%.

00:09:37.161 --> 00:09:41.079
Wearing a hat is going to eliminate all of
that, and that's without even mentioning all

00:09:41.079 --> 00:09:45.700
the other biological ramifications, wearing
a hat basically nerfs all of a cat's hearing

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.700
benefits.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:49.710
And all of this is without even mentioning
the other biological ramifications, like the

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:54.220
fact that cats release a lot of their excess
heat when stressed through their ears, meaning

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:57.230
that Puss is going to be sweltering in any
battle he's in the middle of.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:01.920
All in all, he may look dapper, but that's
a Hat-astrophe that's waiting to happen.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:03.250
Death number four.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:06.079
Similarly Puss’s cape is also going to be
causing him a massive problem.

00:10:06.079 --> 00:10:09.380
For all intents and purposes, the cape is
going to act like a collar, but just much

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.060
more dangerous than a normal collar.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:14.540
See, though, putting a collar on your cat
is usually fine and helps identify your feline

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:15.540
friend to strangers.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:17.510
They can be dangerous in specific situations.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:21.090
If they become snagged on some sort of object,
like a branch or rock, then the cat might

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.589
be choked or strangled.

00:10:22.589 --> 00:10:26.430
The cape is going to present all of the exact
same problems, but ten times worse because

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.780
it's just a bolt of fabric that's hanging
from his neck.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:32.889
Puss’s cape is just an open invitation for
him to be caught and choked, especially in

00:10:32.889 --> 00:10:35.399
a fight with an enemy who's smart enough to
just grab the thing.

00:10:35.399 --> 00:10:38.350
And wouldn’t you know it, that's exactly
what we see happen in this new movie.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:44.530
Honestly, Edna mode from The Incredibles’s
been right about this one for decades.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.530
No capes!

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:46.959
It's death number five.

00:10:46.959 --> 00:10:48.269
No escape for this cape.

00:10:48.269 --> 00:10:50.209
But perhaps the worst in this whole attire?

00:10:50.209 --> 00:10:51.209
The boots.

00:10:51.209 --> 00:10:53.970
You ever notice how cats try to get anything
that's stuck on their feet off?

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:57.899
Puss himself literally does this in the movie
when he's forced to wear those little kitten

00:10:57.899 --> 00:10:58.899
mittens.

00:10:58.899 --> 00:11:00.470
Puss: Stupid Mittens

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.110
Cats don't like having their paws covered
for a lot of reasons.

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:06.079
Some of them are kind of mundane, like the
fact that there are scent glands in their

00:11:06.079 --> 00:11:07.760
paws that help them mark their territory.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:11.190
They're also comforted by needing their little
cat beans on their owners' stomachs.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.700
But other reasons are a lot more serious.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.910
The most obvious one is that paw pads are
a massive shock absorber.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:19.329
They help cats remain quiet and stealthy.

00:11:19.329 --> 00:11:22.570
Cats literally evolved to walk on their toes
so they can move more silently.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:26.450
Changing that up to loud heavy boots click
clacking as Puss moves around is going to

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.746
give up a massive natural advantage that cats
have as fighters.

00:11:29.746 --> 00:11:30.360
Another problem?

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:33.950
Cats actually sweat through their paws, mostly
when they're nervous.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:37.070
Ever take your cat to the vet and notice that
there's damp little footprints everywhere?

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:40.880
So if Puss in Boots ever gets anxious or scared,
he's going to basically be standing in a pool

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.519
of his own sweat in the boots.

00:11:42.519 --> 00:11:45.810
On top of getting himself a case of sweaty
palms and dropping his sword everywhere.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:48.365
Ha, I wonder if we've ever seen that in the
movie.

00:11:57.100 --> 00:12:01.329
But not only is it a problem in battle, it's
also just unhealthy for Puss.

00:12:01.329 --> 00:12:05.010
Sweating helps regulate your body temperature,
cooling you by evaporating on the skin.

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:09.190
This works the same way with the sweat coming
from cat paws, but it simply wouldn't be possible

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:12.780
if two of Puss’s paws were in leather boots
that don't breathe at all.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:15.560
They'd be sticky and gross and wouldn't help
him cool off.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:18.303
And if anyone is in need of staying cool,
it's Puss.

00:12:20.529 --> 00:12:24.510
Without the ability to sweat unimpeded Puss
is running the risk of overheating, especially

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.290
during those anxious fits after he fights
Death.

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:31.480
And on top of all of that, just like the hat
