00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:38.780
It’s not super common knowledge, but cats
actually have tiny tactile hairs between their

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:41.010
pop pads that act similarly to whiskers.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:45.507
These hairs not only act as a protective covering
against debris, chemicals or exposure to the elements.

00:12:45.507 --> 00:12:49.950
But along with nerve receptors in the pads
themselves, they let the cat know a lot about

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.320
the ground that they're walking on.

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:52.630
What sort of material is it?

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:53.630
What's the temperature?

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:57.360
With the boots, he's losing basically all
of the feedback that cats get from their paw

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:59.139
pads and the hairs touching the ground.

00:12:59.139 --> 00:13:02.510
In short, it's a recipe for death number six:
Death in Boots.

